        "id": 1535162
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-03T21:43:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, I do think this is specific to the Microchip MEC series. In their documentation[1] for the MEC152x series of chips, they describe a \"four-byte transfer mode\" where four OS2EC and EC2OS registers are used to communicate with the host.\n\nThis is accompanied by a status register and a command register.\n\n[1]: http://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/en/DeviceDoc/MEC152x-Data-Sheet-DS00003427A.pdf\n\nI\u0027m going to mark this one resolved for now, but I\u0027m of course not terminating the discussion. :)",
